      "date": "2026-10-01T06:30:47.000Z",
      "summary": "Gemini 4 Argon is Google's first frontier model in over seven months. It matches GPT-6 Astra in independent testing but can't keep up with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5. The per-token price is low, but Argon burns through more than twice as many tokens per task as Astra. Select testers get access first, with the API and paid tiers following later. The article Google Gemini 4 Argon closes the gap with OpenAI and Anthrop",
      "why": "The results matter because Argon competes closely with Astra on performance but trails Claude Opus 5.5 and is currently available only to select testers.",
      "headline": "Gemini 4 Argon narrows gap with rivals but doesn't lead",
      "aiSummary": "Independent testing shows Gemini 4 Argon matches GPT-6 Astra but does not keep up with Anthropic’s Claude Opus 5.5. Argon has a low per-token price but consumes more than twice as many tokens per task as Astra, and initial access is limited to select testers with API and paid tiers to follow later."
